Implementation
AircraftBody gains flatten. aircraftPoint() applies foreshortening shared by drawing and support geometry; door and panel bodies begin flattening after contact. Small chip contact uses the rotated lower edge rather than a generic radius.

The aircraft impact rim response is constrained to the impact interval. HypotheticalScenery moves the siege sun and its canal reflection away from the projectile composition.

Adds the helicopter-cinematic-2026-10-19 review page, README, art-study.json, twelve story stills, storyboard and helicopter-sequence.mp4, and links it from the encounter preview. Runtime integration and audio already exist in 4057d1a.

Timing and limitations
The inserted arrival interval is inherited: HELICOPTER_SEQUENCE starts at story tick 304 and reserves 372 ticks at 60 Hz. This commit does not introduce that clock mapping.

The first video is eight seconds at 30 fps from a 60 Hz scene. Later revisions replace footage and metadata; immutable source links below preserve this original version.

